    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/agent_friction.py `resolve_positional_id` accepts any line N that parses and has no `id`. The scenario 'Legacy event identity is stable' (spec.md lines 41-46) covers 'an earlier line was removed', which this cannot honour for positional references. The only guard is the 'has its own id' check.",
      "id": "positional-id-resolves-against-current-file",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "A positional `legacy-N` reference is translated against the current physical line N. If earlier lines have been removed or reordered since it was persisted, it can silently resolve to a different id-less event. The spec says it must resolve to the same identity or fail with a named error."
    },
    {
      "evidence": "template/scripts/agent_friction.py `legacy_content_id` hashes `line.strip()` only. `_parse_log_text` does not de-duplicate or disambiguate repeated ids.",
      "id": "identical-legacy-lines-collide",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The content-derived legacy id is a hash of the stripped line. Two byte-identical id-less lines get the same id, so they merge in route state and attributions. Position-based ids kept them distinct."
    }
  ],
